# Copy to .env.local (Expo loads it automatically and inlines any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ var at build time). Values come from the Supabase dashboard
# → Project Settings → API — the same project the web console uses.
#
# The publishable key is not a secret: it identifies the project and grants
# nothing on its own. Every read and write is decided by row-level security
# against the signed-in user's JWT. Never ship the *secret* (service_role)
# key in an app bundle — it bypasses RLS entirely.
#
# Unlike the Firebase emulator setup this replaces, there is no LAN-IP
# juggling: a device talks to the hosted project directly. To run against a
# local `supabase start` instead, point the URL at your machine's LAN IP on
# port 54321 (localhost won't resolve from a device or the Android
# emulator).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Older projects label the same key "anon"; either name is accepted.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
